    53	# ''One SharedWorker per house.'' A tab knows its face from its custody anchor before it connects, then opens the SharedWorker whose `name` digests that house's (PersonaGroup, persona root); the house's island runs in that worker's own thread and realm, with no nested Worker (Chromium exposes none inside a SharedWorker), so each face keeps its own realm, one island per house, and a house outlives any one of its tabs. Red, in a real browser on every engine: two faces' tabs reach two worker instances, a second tab of one face reaches the same one, and the last tab's close ends the house.
